<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian stocks seen weaker, little to inspire.</title>
<headline>Australian stocks seen weaker, little to inspire.</headline>
<text>
<p>-----------------(Snapshot 8.40 a.m./2240 GMT)-----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	   2673.00  -26.10   DJIA  cl	7922.98   +1.16</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl	 2670	-3   US 30yr cl	 6.55   +0.02</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    93.295  -0.040   Gold NY 319.95 Lon fix 321.70</p>
<p>AUD	   0.7365 (Mon 0.7378)   CRB Index cl   234.51   +0.99</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	20228.72 +353.23   FTSE cl	 4857.40  +57.90</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   926.35   -0.50   NZSE40	  2490.05  -15.27</p>
<p>--------------------------(July 15)----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks seen drifting lower again, little short-term upside seen. &quot;I'm a bit negative on it today, although you may see some bargain hunting,&quot; said Nevitts Ltd senior dealer, Jim Tredenick.  </p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$18.49 (-.01), A$19.56 (-.046), A$6.30 (steady), A$7.71 (-.03)</p>
<p>*Wall Street stocks finished higher with tech stocks extending their torrid run and blue chips scratching out the slenderest of gains.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 18-9/16 (-7/16), BHP 27-7/16 (-11/16), WMC 23-1/16 (-10/16), National Australia Bank 72-11/16 (-1-6/16)</p>
<p>*Gold price was weaker in light volume, on LME copper maintained a firmer tone, zinc hit new highs, rest were mixed.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
